// Nürburgring 24h: Nürburgring, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany
// The 25.4 km lap of the 24 Hours: the Grand Prix circuit (without the Mercedes Arena loop: the 24h variant
// cuts straight through after the first corner) and the whole Nordschleife, 20 km of narrow, hilly road through
// the Eifel woods, nearly 300 m from its lowest point (Breidscheid) to its highest (Hohe Acht), then back onto the
// GP pit straight through the Hohenrain chicane.
// The Grand Prix part has the full circuit look (gravel, sponsor walls, grandstands, the pit building); the
// Nordschleife has only trees: dense woods right behind a steel guardrail a few metres from the white line,
// open fields at Flugplatz and the Döttinger Höhe (forest and meadows below; see forest.js).
// Layout: OpenStreetMap raceways (OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL) via markthebault/open-racetrack-db
//   (24hr layout), converted to metres; within 0.15 m of the source line. Start/finish and the pit lane from
//   OpenStreetMap; section names from the OpenStreetMap ways; corners checked against the track's curvature.
// Elevation: Mapzen Terrain Tiles (Copernicus EU-DEM, SRTM) via open-racetrack-db: the road every 20 m round
//   the lap (smoothed over ~250 m), and the real ground around the circuit on an 85 m grid (`terrain`).
// Every field is explained in _template.js. Distances are metres along the lap from points[0] (the finish line).
